  "idea": {
    "name": "Everything Down Here Makes Its Own Light",
    "premise": "Below the meadow there is a trench the moon cannot reach, and past it an abyssal plain where a drowned lighthouse still turns for ships that will never come. Something out there began to answer every flash, late and in the wrong colour. It is not late any more. It has learned the trench's pattern, the lighthouse's pattern, and yours, and now it answers a half-second before you send, in exactly your colour, so that you can no longer tell which of you is speaking. It has come close. The water that was black is white with it; you are standing inside the reply. The house is about loneliness that learned to glow, and what happens after: being answered so completely that there is no dark left to signal from, and no way to put your light out without it noticing.",
